[Variation "The restrained classical center"]

{ Volume 10: Averbakh and Makogonov Systems. With h3 included, White controls g4 and can develop the bishop freely, while Black gains time for queenside restraint. } 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. h3 O-O 6. Nf3 e5 7. d5 a5 8. Bg5 Na6 9. Nd2 Qe8 { Black plan: Prepare ...Nd7, ...Nh7, or ...c6 and avoid committing the f-pawn without access. White plan: White seeks g4, Be2, and a later queenside break. Decision: Ask whether the first fight is for f5, c5, or the king's destination. Warning: Blindly forcing ...f5 can meet a prepared g4 clamp. Memory: A prevented maneuver is information: choose a different route. } *

