[Variation "Early Bg5"]

{ Volume 11: Early e4 Deviations. White uses the bishop to influence d8-h4 and slow the natural ...e5 break. } 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. Bg5 O-O 6. Qd2 c5 7. d5 e6 { Black plan: Counter with ...c5, question d4, and keep the knight routes flexible. White plan: White may castle long and begin h4-h5. Decision: Read the king placement before choosing which wing to open. Warning: Copying a closed-center attack before the center is closed can expose Black. Memory: An unusual move matters through the plan it enables. } *

