[Variation "The Bd3 setup"]

{ Volume 11: Early e4 Deviations. Bd3 supports the kingside and Nge2 preserves f-pawn mobility, but the pieces can obstruct one another. } 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. Bd3 O-O 6. Nge2 e5 7. d5 c6 8. O-O cxd5 9. cxd5 { Black plan: Challenge the center and make White prove that the setup can coordinate. White plan: White may play f3 or f4 and seek a direct kingside expansion. Decision: Decide whether opening the center exploits White's slower kingside development. Warning: Closing automatically may give White time to arrange the attack. Memory: When White's pieces crowd one wing, open the center if your king is safer. } *

[Event "KID Deep Understanding Course"]
[Site "Study file"]
