[White "Reference line"]
[Black "Black repertoire"]
[Result "*"]
[Variation "Barry and 150-style attack"]

{ Volume 12: Anti-King's Indian Systems. White builds an e4 center without c4 and often plans long castling and h-pawn play. } 1. d4 Nf6 2. Nf3 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. Be3 O-O 6. Qd2 c6 { Black plan: Challenge with ...e5 or ...b5, create an escape route for the queen, and calculate opposite-wing races. White plan: White wants Bh6, long castling, and h4-h5. Decision: Treat the position as a Pirc-like attack with an extra d4 move, not as a closed KID. Warning: Castling into a prepared battery without planning ...c6 or counterplay invites a direct attack. Memory: Similar piece setups can demand different plans when one pawn is missing. } *

