[Black "Black repertoire"]
[Result "*"]
[Variation "English transposition with d4"]

{ Volume 13: English and Reti Transpositions. Once White adds d4 and e4, the normal Classical KID map returns despite the different move order. } 1. c4 Nf6 2. Nc3 g6 3. d4 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. Nf3 O-O 6. Be2 e5 7. O-O { Black plan: Use the same central-break repertoire and identify whether d5 closes the center. White plan: White may exploit move-order details before committing Nf3 or Be2. Decision: Confirm that every piece and pawn has reached the intended version before recalling theory. Warning: Remembering the opening name without checking the exact position causes move-order errors. Memory: Transposition is equality of positions, not similarity of appearance. } *

