[Black "Black repertoire"]
[Result "*"]
[Variation "Botvinnik-style English center"]

{ Volume 13: English and Reti Transpositions. White controls d5 with c4 and e4 but has not played d4, so the central geometry is different from the KID. } 1. c4 Nf6 2. Nc3 g6 3. g3 Bg7 4. Bg2 O-O 5. e4 d6 6. Nge2 e5 7. O-O { Black plan: Challenge d5, use ...c6 or ...Nc6, and consider queenside or kingside play based on pawn locks. White plan: White may play d3, h3, and f4 while keeping d4 flexible. Decision: Do not force ...f5 merely because both sides have fianchettoed. Warning: A KID-looking shell can hide a Botvinnik structure with different breaks. Memory: Count central pawns before naming the plan. } *

