[White "Reference line"]
[Black "Black repertoire"]
[Result "*"]
[Variation "Symmetrical Reti center"]

{ Volume 13: English and Reti Transpositions. With neither c-pawn committed, the game is a maneuvering struggle rather than a standard KID space concession. } 1. Nf3 Nf6 2. g3 g6 3. Bg2 Bg7 4. O-O O-O 5. d3 d6 6. e4 e5 { Black plan: Develop, contest d5 and f5, and choose ...c5 or ...Nc6 according to White's setup. White plan: White may use Nbd2, Re1, and c3 or c4 to build later. Decision: Preserve flexibility until the c-pawns reveal the true structure. Warning: Launching a wing attack while the center can open is premature. Memory: A setup is not a structure until the central pawns speak. } *

